# The firmware the PC image (variant "pc": the macweb recipe for ordinary x86-64 PCs; ./run.sh build-pc-layered) keeps. repack.sh puts
# the whole linux-firmware set into /lib/firmware for that variant and post-build.sh then deletes every file no pattern below matches.
# Same format as mac-firmware.keep: one pattern per line, relative to /lib/firmware, shell globbing where * also matches '/', a kept
# symbolic link keeps its target, '#' lines and blank lines are ignored. crates/iyakki-core/tests/boot_menu.rs checks that the files
# named "required" below stay matched.
#
# What is kept, and why: every GPU a PC can have (the point of this image: docs/GPU-K3S.md), the Wi-Fi, Bluetooth and Ethernet
# chips of ordinary PCs and laptops, the regulatory database. What is dropped: Mac-only Broadcom files that need Apple's firmware,
# single-board-computer and server NIC families (Mellanox, Marvell, Cavium, Chelsio ...), TV tuners, sound DSP images (no SOF driver in
# this kernel), Qualcomm phone/ARM parts, and the NVIDIA GSP 570 files (kernel 6.12's nouveau loads 535.113.01 only; the NVIDIA open
# modules bring their own GSP firmware from the vendor download, never from this image).

# Wireless regulatory database (every Wi-Fi driver).
regulatory.db
regulatory.db.p7s

# ---- GPUs ----
# NVIDIA through nouveau. Turing, Ampere, Ada: the GSP firmware (535.113.01; Ada's and the GA10x entries are links to ga102's files)
# plus the signed boot files; the older generations (Maxwell, Pascal, Volta) have small per-engine files and no GSP.
# required: nvidia/ga102/gsp/gsp-535.113.01.bin nvidia/ad102/gsp/gsp-535.113.01.bin nvidia/tu102/gsp/gsp-535.113.01.bin nvidia/ad102/gsp/booter_load-535.113.01.bin
nvidia/tu1*/gsp/*535.113.01*
nvidia/ga10*/gsp/*535.113.01*
nvidia/ad10*/gsp/*535.113.01*
nvidia/tu1*/acr/*
nvidia/tu1*/gr/*
nvidia/tu1*/nvdec/*
nvidia/tu1*/sec2/*
nvidia/ga10*/acr/*
nvidia/ga10*/gr/*
nvidia/ga10*/nvdec/*
nvidia/ga10*/sec2/*
nvidia/ad10*/acr/*
nvidia/ad10*/gr/*
nvidia/gm*/*
nvidia/gp*/*
nvidia/gv*/*
nvidia/gk20a/*
nvidia/tegra*/*

# AMD graphics: all of amdgpu (GCN to RDNA 4, video decode and the power/display microcontrollers), and radeon for the older cards.
# required: amdgpu/gc_11_0_1_pfp.bin amdgpu/polaris10_mc.bin amdgpu/psp_13_0_4_toc.bin radeon/verde_mc.bin
amdgpu/*
radeon/*
# Not shipped (licence, docs/FIRMWARE-LICENCES.md): amdgpu/isp_* is under LICENSE.amdisp, which allows use only with one APU generation (GFX 11.5.1)
# and is revocable; our kernel has no ISP camera driver for it. A line starting with '!' drops matching files even when a pattern above keeps them.
!amdgpu/isp_*

# Intel graphics: i915 (display microcontroller DMC, GuC, HuC), xe, and the GSC/HDCP parts.
# required: i915/tgl_dmc_ver2_12.bin i915/adlp_guc_70.bin i915/tgl_huc.bin
i915/*
xe/*

# ---- Wi-Fi ----
# Intel iwlwifi is NOT listed here: post-build.sh adds the patterns that iwlwifi-keep.sh derives from the kernel's own MODULE_FIRMWARE
# (the newest file of each chip that the kernel can use, and the one below it; 71 MB instead of 265 MB). Realtek,
# Atheros/Qualcomm and Ralink follow. MediaTek is not here any more: its licence is not an open-source one, so the "MediaTek Wi-Fi and Bluetooth
# firmware" tile (Store, Setup, Hardware: fw-mediatek) installs it at the person's click.
# required: rtw88/rtw8822c_fw.bin rtw89/rtw8852a_fw.bin
rtw88/*
rtw89/*
rtlwifi/*
# Realtek Ethernet over USB (r8152: RTL8153/RTL8156) only. The PCIe files (r8169: LICENSE.r8169, a two-line "hexadecimal or equivalent
# format" permission) are not shipped (docs/RESTRICTED-FIRMWARE.md): the "Realtek network firmware" tile installs them at the person's click.
rtl_nic/rtl8153*
rtl_nic/rtl8156*
ath9k_htc/*
ath10k/*
# Not shipped: the WCN3990 phone-SoC files fall under LICENSE.qcom (no open-source terms on the Materials, Qualcomm chipsets only) and no PC has that chip.
!ath10k/WCN3990/*
# Qualcomm Atheros 11ax/11be: the laptop chips (QCA6390, QCA2066, WCN6855, WCN7850), not the router (IPQ, QCN9274) or phone (WCN6750) ones
ath11k/QCA6390/*
ath11k/QCA2066/*
ath11k/WCN6855/*
ath12k/WCN7850/*
ar3k/*
ath3k-1.fw
ar9170-*.fw
ar9271.fw
ar7010*.fw
# carl9170-1.fw is not shipped: GPL-2.0-or-later with no source offer in linux-firmware (docs/FIRMWARE-LICENCES.md); a tile installs it.
htc_7010.fw
htc_9271.fw
rt2561.bin
rt2561s.bin
rt2661.bin
rt2860.bin
rt2870.bin
rt3070.bin
rt3071.bin
rt3090.bin
rt3290.bin
rt73.bin

# ---- Bluetooth ----
# Intel (ibt-*), Realtek, Qualcomm/Atheros, MediaTek (a download item now, see the top of this file).
# required: intel/ibt-19-0-4.sfi rtl_bt/rtl8761bu_fw.bin
intel/ibt-*
rtl_bt/*
# Qualcomm Atheros Bluetooth: the files under LICENSE.QualcommAtheros_ath10k stay (QCA61x4, QCA9377, WCN399x, WCN6750, QCA2066). The 20 files
# under LICENSE.qcom ("you shall not subject the Materials to any third party license terms (e.g. open source license terms)") are not shipped;
# see the '!' lines at the end of this list and the "Qualcomm Bluetooth firmware" tile (docs/RESTRICTED-FIRMWARE.md).
qca/*

# ---- Ethernet and USB ----
# Realtek (rtl_nic/ above), Intel (e100, igc/e1000e need none), Broadcom (tg3, bnx2, bnx2x), Aquantia, USB 3 host controllers that need a
# firmware file (Renesas uPD720201/2).
# required: rtl_nic/rtl8153b-2.fw e100/d101m_ucode.bin
# Broadcom Ethernet (tigon, bnx2, bnx2x: LICENCE.tigon, LICENCE.bnx2, LICENCE.bnx2x, the same two-line "hexadecimal or equivalent format"
# permission) is not shipped: the "Broadcom Tigon3 network firmware" tile installs it. Without it tg3 works at reduced function; bnx2 and bnx2x
# (server cards) do not start (docs/RESTRICTED-FIRMWARE.md lists what degrades per chip).
e100/*
renesas_usb_fw.mem

# ---- Restricted firmware (docs/RESTRICTED-FIRMWARE.md): never shipped, whatever a pattern above says. post-build.sh also strips every file of
# restricted-firmware.table from the image (all variants), so this list and the table cannot drift apart: a test runs both.
!tigon/*
!bnx2/*
!bnx2x/*
!carl9170-1.fw
!qca/cmbtfw*
!qca/cmnv*
!qca/apbtfw*
!qca/apnv*
!qca/htbtfw*
!qca/htnv*
!qca/hmtbtfw*
!qca/hmtnv*
!qca/QCA6698/*
